          "title": "You'll want to know: ಅನುಮತಿ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅನುಮತಿ (anumati) — \"permission\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅನುಮತಿ (anumati) is Sanskrit for a mind that goes along with you — agreement given rather than merely not refused."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It belongs with ಹೊರಡು from the leave-taking chapter. In a Kannada house you do not simply set out; you ask ಅನುಮತಿ (anumati) of whoever is host, and only then do you say ಹೋಗಿ ಬರುತ್ತೇನೆ. The farewell you learned early has this word standing in front of it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
