          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸಂಕೋಚ (saṅkōca) — \"hesitancy, holding back\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸಂಕೋಚ (saṅkōca) is Sanskrit for a drawing-in, a shrinking — and in Kannada it names the polite reluctance that stops you accepting what you actually want."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is the one word in this chapter you will hear said to you rather than by you. A host feeding an atithi says ಸಂಕೋಚ (saṅkōca) ಬೇಡ, using the refusal-word from the replies chapter to refuse your refusal. Hearing it is the signal to eat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three."
            }
          ]
        },
