          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಂಬಿಕೆ (nambike) — \"trust\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಂಬಿಕೆ (nambike) is native, made out of the everyday word for believing, and it covers both trust in a person and belief in a thing being so."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Set it beside ಗೌರವ from the courtesy chapter. ಗೌರವ can be given to a stranger at once, because it is owed to a position. ನಂಬಿಕೆ (nambike) has to be collected slowly, and no amount of the first turns into the second."
            }
          ]
        },
