        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಸೌಜನ್ಯ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸೌಜನ್ಯ (saujanya) — \"courtesy, good manners\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸೌಜನ್ಯ (saujanya) is Sanskrit, and underneath it is a good person — courtesy named as a quality of the one behaving rather than as a list of rules being followed. That is a real difference, and Kannada means it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is the word for everything this book has been quietly teaching alongside the vocabulary: ಧನ್ಯವಾದ, ದಯವಿಟ್ಟು, ಕ್ಷಮಿಸಿ, ಗೌರವ, ವಂದನೆ, and now the four words in front of this one. ಸೌಜನ್ಯ (saujanya) is the name of the whole habit."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five: ವಿನಂತಿ (vinanti), ಅನುಮತಿ (anumati), ಸಂಕೋಚ (saṅkōca), ನಂಬಿಕೆ (nambike), ಸೌಜನ್ಯ (saujanya). Enough to name what you have been doing since the thank-you word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
